WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
Keep the assessment names and their structures separate.

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:12.335
Word Intelligibility by Picture Identification uses picture choices, with four lists of twenty-five monosyllabic words in the supplied slide.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.920
The child can point instead of repeating aloud.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:24.740
Northwestern University Children’s Perception of Speech also uses picture choices, with fifty monosyllabic nouns in its test material.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:33.520
Early Speech Perception places performance into four categories, moving from no pattern perception to consistent word identification.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.280
GASP lists phoneme detection, word identification, and sentence comprehension.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:50.200
The Developmental Approach to Successful Listening instead names sound awareness, phonetic listening, and auditory comprehension, and has both assessment and training uses.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:57.780
Finally, Ling sounds can support detection, discrimination, or identification, depending on the response you request.

00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:02.545
They do not establish comprehension of a meaningful message.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:08.700
Vary the order, include silent trials, and document distance and device conditions.

00:01:09.495 --> 00:01:16.775
A change from the child's earlier reliable performance calls for investigation, not a diagnosis from one check.

